        <item>
            <title>1.3.35</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 09:51:07 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>10335</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.35</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 1.3.35</h2>
<ul>
  <li>After the latest Claude app update, the AI tab said "Claude is not installed". MotionUI finds Claude Code in its new place again.</li>
  <li>Figma import keeps blend modes on layers and fills, so glass and other materials blend with what sits behind them, like in Figma.</li>
  <li>Text in a fixed-width box keeps the line breaks it has in Figma.</li>
  <li>Claude can save your After Effects project, so Premiere Pro picks up changes through Dynamic Link without you pressing Cmd+S.</li>
  <li>With Premiere Pro open, Claude could end up working in the hidden After Effects that Premiere starts in the background instead of yours. Fixed.</li>
  <li>If the connection between Claude and After Effects stops, an open MotionUI panel now restarts it on its own.</li>
  <li>The info markers in the app show their text once instead of twice.</li>
  <li>After Effects panel 1.6.14 and Figma plugin 23. After the update, close and reopen MotionUI Agent in Figma once.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
